    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n70123" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεκρ-όω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>make dead, mortify,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μόριόν τι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
					11.265
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νενεκρῶσθαι τὸ μόριον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					18(1).156
				</span></i>
			: metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ δόγματα . . δύναται νεκρωθῆναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					M.Ant.
					7.2
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐ ψυχὴ κυρίως, ἀλλὰ νενεκρωμένη τις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Simp.
					<u>in Ph.</u>
					1066.27
				</span></i>
			; <i>to be dead,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεκρωθείς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					14.1976
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νενεκρωμένος,</span> of the body
			of Abraham, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ep.Rom.</u>
				4.19
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> metaph.,
				<i>mortify,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεκρώσατε τὰ μέλη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Ep.Col.</u>
					3.5
				</span></i>
			.</div>
